    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="13">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:LeisWl">Leis Wl</ref> 13</head>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="xno" source="#robertson" n="13" corresp="#wit-hk">Autersi ki faus jugement fait, pert sa were s'il ne pot jurer sur seinz que mieuz nel sout juger.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-hk">Likewise, he who gives a false judgment shall forfeit his wergeld, unless he can swear on the holy relics that he did not know how to give a better decision.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="501"><ref target="clause:IICn_15-1">II Cn 15.1</ref>; <ref target="clause:LeisWl_39-1">Leis Wl 39.1</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">II Cn. 15, 1 Hs. A | vgl. u. 39, 1</note>
        <note type="editorial">Added October 2026 from Robertson pp. 258–259 (text and translation); Liebermann’s text (K–M) not yet added</note>
      </div>
